    {"id":"nmobbz0z1am1","type":"commentNode","position":{"x":-1480,"y":-460},"data":{"text":"To make a generalized model of 1D Elementary CA in which the user defines the rules of transition based on the traditional binary representation, I organized it in this unoptimized \"mutex-like\" way, to let the user choose via Simulator (using model attributes) if each rule case should yield a cell alive or dead.\n\nAs GenesisCA is fundamentally 2D, I used a neighborhood that look to the two side cells plus itself, and I added the \"Computing Row\" bool attribute, to avoid reprocessing cells that have already been defined. This way, the \"history\" of the 1D generations is preserved as the CA steps each generation","width":423,"height":236,"color":"#57582c"}},
    {"id":"nmp53m7wcdj1","type":"caNode","position":{"x":-1060,"y":-160},"data":{"nodeType":"getCellAttribute","config":{"attributeId":"alive"},"isCollapsed":true}},
